  "afd": {
    "available": true,
    "issued_at": "2026-10-05T07:40:00+00:00",
    "product_id": "befdd536-8d41-4c0d-86a6-4f43842804b4",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 050740\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1240 AM PDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Above-normal temperatures will continue across the region through \n  Friday, with dangerous heat expected in Death Valley.\n\n* Our next system is expected to bring cooler temperatures,\n  increased winds and low precipitation chances this weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Sunday.\n\nRidging and anomalous 500mb heights remain in place through the work \nweek. A weak disturbance can be seen in water vapor satellite \nimagery coming ashore in central/northern CA. This feature will pass \nthrough the southern Great Basin today and then into AZ on Tuesday. \nOnly expecting subtle cooling (1-3 degrees), slightly increased \nbreezes, and a few high clouds today and Tuesday. However, \ntemperatures remain above normal and the ridge quickly rebounds mid-\nweek. Highs are forecast to be 5-12 degrees above normal throughout \nthe week, with the most pronounced heat in the lower elevations of \nDeath Valley National Park where an Extreme Heat Warning is in \neffect through Friday evening. Highs there will be ~110 with \novernight lows in the 80s, resulting in major to extreme HeatRisk. \nElsewhere, anticipating minor to moderate HeatRisk throughout the\nweek.\n\nThis weekend, a Pacific trough is forecast to approach our region. \nUncertainty remains in the trough's interaction with Hurricane \nRachel in the eastern Pacific. The GFS ensemble is more skeptical \nthan the ECMWF ensemble, but rain chances remain on the table on \nSunday and into early next week (10-30%). Confidence is much higher \nin the presence of gusty winds and a cooldown beginning Saturday. \nChances for 30+ mph gusts are 40-75% across most of the area over \nthe weekend, with the best odds of wind impacts generally along the \nI-15 and I-40 corridors. From Friday to Sunday, temperatures are \nforecast to drop ~10 degrees, bringing values back closer to normal. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Light \nwinds following typical directional patterns expected through Monday \nnight. Due to the light magnitude, the direction may vary at times, \nbut will favor the east-northeast during the afternoon. Can't rule \nout an isolated gust to 15 kts (20 percent chance) with the heating \nof the day. No operationally significant cloud cover through the TAF \nperiod.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Light winds following \ntypical directional patterns expected through Monday night. Can't \nrule out isolated gusts between 15 and 20 kts with afternoon \nheating. With these gusts, the Las Vegas Valley TAF sites will favor \nthe east, KBIH the south-southeast, and KDAG the east. No \noperationally significant cloud cover through the TAF period.\n&&\n\n.CLIMATE...Numerous climate locations have a forecast high\ntemperature and/or forecast warm low temperature within 3 degrees of \nthe daily record.\n\nThe table below shows the daily record maximum temperature and the \nyear the record was last set. An asterisk (*) denotes which records \nare in jeopardy (within 3 degrees of the forecast).\n\nMAX           MON, OCT 5  TUE, OCT 6  WED, OCT 7  THU, OCT 8 \n              Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)  Record (Yr)\n\nLas Vegas     100(2024)   100(2024)   99(1978)*   98(2024)* \nBishop        94(1987)    94(2024)*   94(1965)*   95(1996) \nNeedles       112(1917)   111(2024)   107(2024)   107(2024) \nDaggett       104(2024)   105(2024)   102(2024)   101(1996)* \nKingman       99(2024)    100(2024)   99(2024)    98(1996) \nDesert Rock   100(2024)   100(2024)   99(2024)    98(1996)* \nDeath Valley  113(2024)   110(2024)*  109(2024)*  112(1996)*\n\nThe table below shows the daily record warm minimum temperature and \nthe year the record was last set. An asterisk (*) denotes which \nrecords are in jeopardy (within 3 degrees of the forecast).\n\nWARM MIN      MON, OCT 5  TUE, OCT 6  WED, OCT 7  THU, OCT 8 \n              Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)  Record (Yr)\n\nLas Vegas     78(2024)    74(2024)*   75(2024)*   76(2024)* \nBishop        56(1993)    52(2018)    57(1943)    51(1960)* \nNeedles       79(1993)    77(2023)*   76(1947)*   76(2024)* \nDaggett       75(2024)    75(2024)    72(2024)*   69(1980)* \nKingman       67(1924)    67(1949)*   69(1947)*   67(1960)* \nDesert Rock   69(2024)*   66(1990)*   65(1980)*   70(2024)* \nDeath Valley  85(2024)*   83(1943)*   80(1943)*   85(1964)* \n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Woods\nAVIATION...Soulat\nCLIMATE...Soulat\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
